language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ A hiker chooses items to put in a backpack, each with a value and a weight, to maximise the total value without exceeding the weight capacity.
given values_dim1 : int
given values : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1)] of int
given weights : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1)] of int
given capacity : int
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1)] of bool
find total : int(0..100000000)

branching on [x]

maximising total
such that
$ the total weight of the chosen items must not exceed the capacity of the backpack
(sum i : int(1..values_dim1) . x[i] * weights[i]) <= capacity,
$ the total is the summed value of the chosen items
total = (sum i : int(1..values_dim1) . x[i] * values[i])
